WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
September 1932.

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:06.640
In Yerwada jail, Gandhi
begins a fast unto death.

3
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:11.290
His target is a British plan giving
Dalit voters separate electorates.

4
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.490
Ambedkar supported that plan.

5
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.960
Both men opposed untouchability.

6
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.760
Yet here they stood on opposite sides.

7
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:23.760
So why did two opponents of untouchability
disagree so sharply about how to end

8
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:24.460
it?

9
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.760
In this mission, you'll read one verse of
the Bhagavad Gita that the two men read

10
00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:30.640
in very different ways.

11
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.950
Then you'll follow the Dalit
movements that came after them,

12
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.910
and weigh up which approach changed most.

13
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.330
Your mission: explain why Gandhi and
Ambedkar disagreed so sharply about ending

14
00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:43.380
untouchability.
